---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Legal and takedown process" description="Legal notice, takedown, and correction process for streisandeffect.org.">
  <section class="prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal process</p>
    <h1>Takedown and correction requests</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page is a working policy scaffold. It should be reviewed before launch, especially before publishing copyrighted downloads.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section callout warning">
    <h2>Not legal advice</h2>
    <p>
      This project should consult counsel before public launch. The policy below is an operational starting point for public-interest archive handling, not legal advice.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Archive position</h2>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>The archive preserves documents for research, criticism, accountability, and historical record.</li>
      <li>Hosting a file does not imply endorsement of its claims, framing, or conclusions.</li>
      <li>The archive will review valid legal notices and credible correction requests.</li>
      <li>The archive may contest false, abusive, or viewpoint-discriminatory takedown demands.</li>
      <li>The archive may publish transparency information about requests when safe and lawful.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>What to include in a request</h2>
    <p>Send enough information for a human review:</p>
    <ul class="kicker-list">
      <li>Your name and organization, if applicable.</li>
      <li>The exact streisandeffect.org URL at issue.</li>
      <li>The exact file or statement you are challenging.</li>
      <li>Whether the request is legal, copyright, privacy, safety, factual correction, or contextual correction.</li>
      <li>Evidence supporting the request.</li>
      <li>The specific action requested: correction, added context, temporary disabling, removal, or replacement.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Contact:</strong> legal contact pending.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose">
    <h2>Review process</h2>
    <ol class="kicker-list">
      <li>Acknowledge receipt when practical.</li>
      <li>Preserve the request, cited URLs, and current metadata state.</li>
      <li>Check whether the request identifies a real legal or factual issue.</li>
      <li>Decide whether to correct metadata, add context, temporarily disable downloads, reject the request, or seek counsel.</li>
      <li>Record the outcome for the transparency log when appropriate.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
